<title>USA: BASF to defend itself in patent suit.</title>
<headline>BASF to defend itself in patent suit.</headline>
<dateline>MOUNT OLIVE, N.J. 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>BASF AG said Monday it will defend its position that it has not violated any of Optical Coating Laboratory Inc's patents.</p>
<p>Optical Coating said earlier today that it filed a lawsuit against BASF and its U.S. subsidiary, BASF Corp, alleging the company violated a patent that covers optically variable thin film flakes which, when mixed with paints and inks, produce color shifting visual properties.</p>
<p>Optical Coating alleges the patent was infringed when BASF started marketing a pigment in the U.S. for use in automotive paints and other applications.</p>
<p>BASF said in a statement that it is confident about the outcome of the case, but it will offer no further comment about the matter.</p>
</text>
